[ti:Kitchen Light]
[ar:Ilse Norrland]
[al:Small Hours]
[by:Vela demo — original lyrics]

[00:06.67]Kitchen light left on for me
[00:10.00]Kettle ticking, half past three
[00:13.33]You fell asleep with the radio low
[00:16.67]And I came home the long way, slow
[00:20.00]Nothing in this house is new
[00:23.33]Except the way I look at you
[00:26.67]Chairs that creak and doors that stick
[00:30.00]The clock that's always running quick
[00:33.33]Leave the kitchen light on, I'll find my way
[00:40.00]Past the coats and the shoes and the things we didn't say
[00:46.67]Leave the kitchen light on, gold on the floor
[00:53.33]I don't need the whole house, I just need the door
[01:00.00]Bread on the counter, salt in the air
[01:03.33]Your reading glasses on the stair
[01:06.67]The years get quiet, the rooms get small
[01:10.00]Still the brightest thing in the hall
[01:13.33]Leave the kitchen light on, I'll find my way
[01:20.00]Past the coats and the shoes and the things we didn't say
[01:26.67]Leave the kitchen light on, gold on the floor
[01:33.33]I don't need the whole house, I just need the door
